# Test fixture photos are REAL CAMERA FILES carrying GPS coordinates, camera
# model and capture timestamps. They are deliberately not committed — see
# tests/fixtures/images/README.md. Suites that need them skip when absent.
tests/fixtures/images/*.HEIC
tests/fixtures/images/*.heic
tests/fixtures/images/*.jpeg
tests/fixtures/images/*.jpg
tests/fixtures/images/*.png

# EXCEPTION: files ending -scrubbed have been through scripts/scrub-fixture.mjs,
# which strips GPS, the Apple MakerNote (including the per-photo PhotoIdentifier
# UUID), serial numbers and capture timestamps, then FAILS unless it can prove
# none survived. What it deliberately keeps is EXIF Orientation and the
# container's irot transform — the two things that caught D-30 and D-34, and
# without which the fixture would test nothing.
#
# Committing one lets a fresh clone and CI exercise the flagship HEIC path
# instead of skipping it (docs/12 D-36, D-62).
#
# Anything matching this pattern is PUBLIC. Run the script, and check the photo
# does not show a face or an identifiable place — the scrub removes metadata,
# never image content.
!tests/fixtures/images/*-scrubbed.HEIC

# Marketing screenshots from scripts/make-screenshots.mjs. Regenerable from any
# build in one command, never served to anyone, and 1 MB of PNG that would churn
# on every UI change. Unlike public/og/default.png these are not shipped.
screenshots/
